The elixir burns like fire through your veins. You are healed. The poison is gone, but at the cost of Galahad's life.	解藥如烈火般燒遍你的血脈。你痊癒了。毒素已經清除，但代價是葛拉漢的性命。
Wait! Here lies Sir Galahad, purest of your knights. He has also been bitten and is at death's very door.	且慢！葛拉漢爵士就躺在此處，他是你麾下最純潔的騎士。他也遭到咬傷，已是命懸一線。
If you do not give him the elixir, he will die. He could die at any moment! A terrible choice is before you.	若不將解藥給他，他必死無疑。他隨時都可能斷氣！一個可怕的抉擇擺在你面前。
If you drink the elixir, you let Galahad die. If you give Galahad the elixir, your one chance is to find the Grail before your own time runs out.	若你飲下解藥，便是任由葛拉漢死去。若你把解藥給了葛拉漢，你唯一的生機，便是趕在自己時限用盡前尋得聖杯。
Only the healing powers of the Grail may be able to save you. If not, at least Galahad would remain alive to carry on the mission.	唯有聖杯的療癒之力或許能救你一命。若不成，至少葛拉漢仍能存活，繼續完成這項使命。
He is in a healing trance, unable to hear, speak or move.	他正處於療癒的昏迷之中，無法聽聞、言語或動彈。
He cannot use it now. You had best keep it.	他此刻無法使用它，你最好還是留著。
He is unable to eat it and you may yet have need of it.	他無法食用它，而你或許還用得上。
I would not part with it just yet. You may well need it.	我勸你先別捨棄它，你很可能還會用到。
That would not help him.	那對他毫無幫助。
Truly, you are noble. But you must make the clear the nature of the sacrifice you intend.	你確實高潔。但你必須先弄清楚自己打算做出的犧牲，究竟是什麼性質。
Arthur....my king. I knew....you would....come.	亞瑟……吾王。我早知……你會……前來。
Only way out....the gift....for Aphrodite....you must....bring her....bring her the.....	唯一的出路……那份獻禮……獻給阿芙羅黛蒂……你必須……帶給她……帶給她那……
He has lapsed into a healing coma. By the time he is healed, you will be dead of the rat's poison.	他已陷入療癒性昏迷。等他痊癒之時，你早已因鼠毒而喪命。
You have but one chance--to find the Grail! Only its healing powers may yet save you....if you can find it in time.	你只剩一個機會——尋得聖杯！唯有它的療癒之力或許還能救你……前提是你能及時尋得。
Do not despair or regret your choice. You have done the good and noble deed and saved Galahad, who served you so faithfully.	莫要絕望，也莫要懊悔你的抉擇。你做了良善而高潔的事，救了對你忠心耿耿的葛拉漢。
Alas! A rat has bitten you! There was nothing you could do to avoid it.	唉！一隻老鼠咬傷了你！這是你避無可避之事。
The hierophant warned that even one bite was lethal and death inevitable, though it may be slow in coming.	祭司曾警告，即便只是一口咬傷也是致命的，死亡無可避免，只是來得或許緩慢。
And it appears that Galahad has fallen prey to the rats, for there he lies upon a bier, unaware even of your presence.	看來葛拉漢也已成為鼠群的獵物，此刻他躺在靈架上，甚至渾然不覺你在此處。
Nay, you chose wrongly! Now you are trapped within this room. By the time Galahad recovers, he will find you dead.	不，你選錯了！如今你被困在這房間裡。等葛拉漢康復之時，見到的將是你的屍身。
I cannot bear to remain and watch. At least you die knowing that Galahad will live to carry on the mission, for the Goddess has sworn to release him. Farewell, Arthur.	我不忍留下來看著。至少你臨死之際能知曉，葛拉漢將活下去繼續這項使命，因為女神已立誓要釋放他。永別了，亞瑟。
Never have I felt such contempt for you as I do at this moment. You have chosen your own life over that of Galahad and now he is dead.	我從未如此刻這般鄙夷你。你選擇了保全自己的性命而非葛拉漢，如今他已死去。
The elixir burns through your body, purging the poison. You are healed in body, but your soul is forever tainted.	解藥燒遍你的全身，滌淨了毒素。你的肉身痊癒了，靈魂卻永遠蒙上污點。
Galahad is dead. You have failed to save one of your greatest and purest knights. This is a grievous failure on your part.	葛拉漢死了。你未能救下麾下最偉大、最純潔的騎士之一，這是你莫大的失職。
Arthur, Galahad grows much worse! I fear he is about to die!	亞瑟，葛拉漢的情況急轉直下！我恐怕他就要死了！
Do not go too close, Arthur, I beg you! a ghoul is not to be trusted.	亞瑟，求你別靠得太近！食屍鬼不可信任。
You will learn nothing from this long-dead fiend in the sarcophagus.	從石棺裡這具早已作古的邪物身上，你什麼也問不出來。
Below the pentacle are carved these words...	五芒星下方刻著這些文字……
Cursed is the priest who lies here. He betrayed the Goddess and stole her treasures. Sacred objects of gold he has stolen.	長眠於此的祭司受了詛咒。他背叛女神，竊取她的寶物，偷走了聖潔的黃金聖物。
By the sign of the pentacle, he is imprisoned. The star of the Goddess rules him. Take heed, you who read these words of warning.	憑五芒星的印記，他被囚禁於此。女神之星統御著他。讀到這則警語的人啊，務必當心。
The light is too dim to make out the inscription from here.	光線太暗，從這裡看不清銘文。
The lid of the sarcophagus is closed.	石棺的蓋子是闔上的。
You cannot look inside it from here and I do not advise getting closer.	你從這裡看不進去，我也不建議你靠得更近。
That is quite impossible. It is solid stone.	那絕無可能，它是實心的石頭。
There is nothing upon the other side of the sarcophagus but a blank wall.	石棺的另一側除了一面空牆，什麼也沒有。
There are three doorways and colorful patterns upon the walls. There are no mummies or funeral urns here, only the one large, stone sarcophagus.	這裡有三道門，牆上繪著色彩繽紛的圖案。此處沒有木乃伊或骨灰甕，只有一具巨大的石棺。
What ARE you babbling about?	你究竟在胡言亂語些什麼？
Nay, Arthur! Let your curiosity rest. Draw no closer, I beg you!	不，亞瑟！按捺你的好奇心吧。求你別再靠近了！
It crouches in the dark end of the sarcophagus, gibbering, grinding its hideous teeth and smelling of putrefaction, a vile and demented creature.	牠蜷伏在石棺陰暗的一端，喃喃自語，磨著猙獰的牙齒，散發腐爛的氣味，是個邪惡而瘋狂的生物。
Whatever its origins, it is clearly evil and hungers for that which is still alive.	不論牠的來歷為何，牠顯然邪惡，渴求著仍有生氣之物。
It is solid stone, carved with geometric designs on the sides. There is something different upon the lid, however.	它是實心石材，側面刻著幾何圖案。不過蓋子上頭有些不同的東西。
There is a pentacle carved upon it and an inscription in Latin below that.	上面刻著一枚五芒星，下方還有一段拉丁文銘文。
The light is too dim to make it out from here.	光線太暗，從這裡看不清楚。
It is the five-pointed star or pentacle that is associated with the Goddess.	那是與女神相關聯的五芒星，即五角星形。
And because it is formed of one unbroken line, it is used to keep out harmful spirits. Or to lock them in.	由於它是由一筆不間斷的線畫成，因此可用來擋住有害的鬼靈，或是將牠們封鎖在內。
There are many colourful geometric patterns painted upon the walls and doorways.	牆上與門邊繪著許多色彩繽紛的幾何圖案。
One wall has geometric designs painted upon it and a pentacle over one door. The other three walls are barren.	一面牆上繪有幾何圖案，其中一道門上方有一枚五芒星，其餘三面牆則空無一物。
It is...well, frankly, Arthur, I do not know what it is. I do not know EVERYTHING.	那是……嗯，老實說，亞瑟，我也不知道那是什麼。我並非無所不知。
There are some support beams sticking out of the wall over one door.	有幾根支撐橫樑從一道門上方的牆裡凸出。
The lid is under the control of the Thing inside. I guarantee you could not move it.	蓋子受裡頭那東西所掌控，我敢保證你根本移不動它。
It IS shut.	它確實是關著的。
The stone lid is heavy and undoubtedly better left in place.	石蓋十分沉重，無疑最好別去動它。
The thing in the sarcophagus wants nothing further to do with you, fortunately.	所幸，石棺裡的那東西不想再與你有任何瓜葛。
Merely possessing the medallion is protection enough. The fiend will know it is there.	光是持有這條六角星項鍊便足以自保，那邪物會知曉它的存在。
It is more likely to get you, were you to attempt such folly.	你若貿然做出這等蠢事，牠反倒更可能捉住你。
The sarcophagus is closed.	石棺是闔上的。
If what you seek is in the sarcophagus, it is guarded by the Thing.	你若尋找的東西在石棺裡，那便有那東西看守著。
There was but one and you took it.	那裡原本只有一個，已被你取走。
Impractical, not to mention impossible.	不切實際，更別說根本不可能。
You cannot kill that which is already dead.	你殺不死早已死去之物。
Yes, come closer. I will show you my golden treasure. Do not be afraid.	是啊，再靠近些。我會讓你瞧瞧我的黃金寶藏，不必害怕。
I wish only to smell more of your warm blood, to hear the rhythm of living breath in your lungs. That is all. Come closer.	我只想再多嗅幾分你溫熱的血氣，聽一聽你肺裡活人呼吸的節奏。僅此而已，再靠近些。
Sssssst! Begone! The accursed Goddess protects you. Begone! 	嘶嘶嘶！滾開！那該死的女神在庇護著你。滾開！ 
Your source of protection? Are you mad!?	你的護身之物？你瘋了嗎！？
How could I have raised you to be such a fool?	我怎會把你養育成這般愚笨之人？
Arthur, do not tempt fate by trifling with this ghoul.	亞瑟，別拿這隻食屍鬼來試探命運。
There is nothing left to get.	已經沒有東西可拿了。
The Thing drank it then ate the glass vial.	那東西喝下了它，接著連玻璃瓶一起吞下。
Without the medallion around your neck, you are no longer protected from the Thing. You were a fool to part with it.	沒了掛在頸間的六角星項鍊，你便不再受那東西的庇護。捨棄它實在愚蠢。
Screeeeeaaaagh! The accursed pentacle!	嘎啊啊啊啊！那該死的五芒星！
The Thing has retreated from the warding spell of the medallion. There is a glint of gold at this end of the sarcophagus.	那東西已被六角星項鍊的護符之力逼退。石棺這一端閃著一絲金光。
I believe....aye, it is a golden apple.	我想……沒錯，那是一顆金蘋果。
An apple of solid gold! I wonder how often the fiend has used it as a lure.	一顆純金打造的蘋果！不知那邪物用它當誘餌，騙過了多少次。
Hang onto it this time, Arthur.	這次好好留著它，亞瑟。
Alas, curiosity killed the King. Even the worms will go hungry by the time the ghoul is finished with you.	唉，好奇心害死了國王。等那食屍鬼把你解決掉時，連蛆蟲都要餓肚子了。
I smell warm blood and live flesh. Come closer. I have golden treasure. Come closer and see.	我嗅到了溫熱的血與活人的肉。再靠近些。我有黃金寶藏，靠近來瞧瞧。
The sound of the Thing gnashing at your apple is truly revolting. And what a waste of the Seeress' gift!	那東西啃咬你那顆蘋果的聲音，實在令人作嘔。這下白白浪費了女預言家的贈禮！
The Thing devours the elixir, vial and all. That was truly a foolilsh move. It does the creature no good, but leaves you with no protection from rat bite.	那東西把解藥連瓶子一併吞下。這一步實在愚蠢，對那生物毫無益處，卻讓你失去了對抗鼠咬的防護。
I cannot imagine what possessed you to do such a mindless thing.	我實在想不透，是什麼鬼迷心竅讓你做出這種蠢事。
From the sound of the ghoul's gnashing teeth, I would say it enjoyed even that old bone. Imagine how much more he would enjoy your own, fresh bones.	聽那食屍鬼磨牙的聲音，我猜牠連那根舊骨頭都吃得津津有味。可以想見，牠會有多麼享用你那新鮮的骨頭。
The Thing in the sarcophagus wants nothing further to do with you, fortunately.	所幸，石棺裡的那東西不想再與你有任何瓜葛。
The stairs lead upward.	這道階梯通往上方。
There are two doorways to this room.	這房間有兩道門。
A mural covers one entire wall. There are two doorways, mummies and painted designs, including many spirals.	一整面牆繪滿了壁畫。這裡有兩道門、數具木乃伊，以及包括許多螺形紋飾在內的彩繪圖案。
There are lunar and solar spirals here. A solar spiral goes in the sunwise direction. Sunwise is the direction that the shadow of the sun moves around a sundial.	這裡有太陽螺紋與月亮螺紋。太陽螺紋依順日方向盤繞，順日方向即是日晷上日影移動的方向。
A lunar spiral moves to the left, in the opposite or counter-sunwise direction.	月亮螺紋則向左盤繞，與順日方向相反，即逆日方向。
Solar spirals are signs of a God, while lunar spirals are signs of a Goddess.	太陽螺紋是男神的標識，月亮螺紋則是女神的標識。
This mural shows the death of Hippolytus, as brought about by Aphrodite. The full story is told in your Liber ex Doctrina.	這幅壁畫描繪的是希波萊特斯之死，正是阿芙羅黛蒂一手造成。完整故事記載於你的《Liber ex Doctrina》之中。
This poor warrior had his head split in two.   He must have lain there for centuries. We shall never know his story.	這名可憐的戰士頭顱被劈成兩半，想必已在此躺了數個世紀，他的故事我們永遠無從得知。
The skeletons of the mummies remain well wrapped.	這些木乃伊的骸骨依舊包裹得完好。
It was split in half by some powerful blow from a large sword. A helmet would have saved him.	它是被某柄大劍的一記重擊劈成兩半的，若有頭盔或許能保住他一命。
All the skulls in this room are well-wrapped... which is sometimes more than I can say for yours.	這房裡所有的頭骨都包裹得很好……有時候，我對你的腦袋可就沒把握這麼說了。
To learn more about what the mural shows, read the Liber ex Doctrina.	想多了解這幅壁畫描繪的內容，去讀《Liber ex Doctrina》吧。
It is quite old, but intact, though not as good as what you have.	它相當古老，卻依然完整，只是比不上你手上那件。
The only armour here is upon your person.	這裡唯一的甲冑，就穿在你自己身上。
A secret exit has opened in the mural. This is now the only way out.	壁畫中開啟了一道密門，如今這是唯一的出路。
One wall is covered with the mural, with four spirals in the corners. There are more spirals upon another wall, and some geometric designs on the other doorway.	一面牆被壁畫覆蓋，四個角落各有一枚螺形紋飾。另一面牆上還有更多螺形紋飾，另一道門邊則繪有幾何圖案。
Other than the spirals and mural, the other decorations are simply painted geometric designs.	除了螺形紋飾與壁畫之外，其餘裝飾都只是彩繪的幾何圖案。
The way is open. Surely the end of your mission draws nigh.	通路已開。你此行的終點，想必已經不遠了。
Nay, let it lie undisturbed any further. The way is open. Press onward.	不，就讓它繼續安眠吧。通路已開，繼續前行。
It is old and far inferior to your own.	它十分老舊，遠遠比不上你自己那件。
The tunnel has brought you to this room. In the wall behind you, the hidden door seals. You cannot even see where it was.	甬道將你帶到了這房間。你身後的牆上，那道密門已經封閉，你甚至看不出它原本在哪裡。
Heavy stone doors have sealed the room! Has the Goddess trapped you or---nay. Look!	沉重的石門已將這房間封死！難道是女神把你困在此處，還是——不，你看！
Secret stairs leading upward have been revealed....along with the skeleton of a warrior.	一道通往上方的密梯顯露出來……旁邊還有一具戰士的骸骨。
You should not be trapped in 73	你不該被困在 73 裡
This room is smaller and more barren, except for the mural upon one wall. The opposite wall has partially collapsed. There are no mummies or urns here.	這房間較小也更為空蕩，除了一面牆上的壁畫之外別無他物。對面的牆壁已部分崩塌，這裡沒有木乃伊或骨灰甕。
It shows the story of Pygmalion, which is written in your Liber ex Doctrina. This version is rather fancifully embellished with doves and piping satyrs.	它描繪的是皮格梅里恩的故事，記載於你的《Liber ex Doctrina》之中。這個版本添了不少幻想的點綴，畫著鴿子與吹笛的森林之神。
Except for the one mural, the other walls are bare. Part of the wall opposite the mural has crumbled away.	除了那幅壁畫之外，其餘牆面都光禿禿的。壁畫對面的牆壁有一部分已經崩落。
I suppose the satyr figures in the mural represent the nature god, Pan, playing upon his pipes.	我猜壁畫裡吹著笛子的森林之神形象，代表的是自然之神潘恩。
There are doves shown in the mural, representing the power of Aphrodite.	壁畫中畫著幾隻鴿子，代表阿芙羅黛蒂的力量。
The stone dove you now carry is much like the doves painted in the mural.	你此刻攜帶的石鴿，與壁畫中所繪的鴿子十分相似。
It is merely a decorative element in the mural.	那不過是壁畫中的裝飾元素罷了。
To learn more of this legend, read the Liber ex Doctrina.	想多了解這則傳說，去讀《Liber ex Doctrina》吧。
There is an inverted cross above one door. The Christians call it St. Peter's Cross, for they believe the apostle Peter was crucified upside-down.	一道門上方有一個倒十字。基督徒稱之為聖彼得十字，因為他們相信使徒彼得是被倒釘十字架而死。
There are some geometric designs painted in one doorway.	一道門邊繪著幾個幾何圖案。
There is nothing there.	那裡什麼也沒有。
Behind and to each side of the statue, hidden doors have opened.	雕像的背後與兩側，都出現了敞開的密門。
It is utterly empty except for a statue of Aphrodite.	這裡空無一物，只有一尊阿芙羅黛蒂的雕像。
This room holds only the statue of Aphrodite and now has a total of four doors from which to choose.	這房間只有阿芙羅黛蒂的雕像，如今共有四道門可供選擇。
There is a stone statue of Aphrodite in the center of the room. Upon one hand rests a carved dove, but the other hand, though held out with palm open, is empty.	房間正中央立著一尊阿芙羅黛蒂的石像。一手擱著一隻雕鑿的鴿子，另一手雖攤開手掌伸出，卻空無一物。
The statue of Aphrodite now holds the apple which has turned to stone in its hand.	阿芙羅黛蒂的雕像手中，如今握著那顆已化為石頭的蘋果。
The walls are completely blank.	牆壁完全是空白的。
What seemed to be blank walls have revealed three hidden doors.	原本看似空白的牆壁，如今顯露出三道密門。
Only half of the doorway into the room is left for part of the wall has crumbled away.	通往這房間的門洞只剩一半，因為牆壁有一部分已經崩塌。
With the exception of the doorway through which you entered, the other doorways are utterly black inside and it is impossible to tell what might lie within.	除了你進來時經過的那道門之外，其餘門內一片漆黑，完全看不出裡頭有什麼。
I cannot imagine why you think the Goddess herself would answer you.	我實在想不透，你為何認為女神本尊會親自回應你。
The statue shows no sign of answering.	雕像沒有任何回應的跡象。
The statue of Aphrodite has a dove upon her hand. Doves are considered one of her fertility symbols.	阿芙羅黛蒂的雕像手上停著一隻鴿子。鴿子被視為她的生育象徵之一。
The statue's instructions were to use the dove after you had proven yourself with sword and shield.	雕像的指示是：待你以劍與盾證明自己之後，再使用那隻鴿子。
I shall attempt to recall the directions: six doors must be entered in this order: west, east, south, east, south, north.	我試著回想那些方向：六道門必須依此順序進入：西、東、南、東、南、北。
